        ("Choose the correct conjunction: She sings ___ she dances at the same time.", ["but","while","because","unless"], "while", "'While' indicates two simultaneous actions.", ["subordinating","simultaneous"]),
        ("Choose the correct conjunction: I brought an umbrella ___ it might rain.", ["because","although","in case","unless"], "in case", "'In case' means as a precaution against the possibility.", ["subordinating","precaution"]),
        ("Choose the correct conjunction: He failed the exam ___ he did not study.", ["although","because","unless","while"], "because", "'Because' gives the reason for failing.", ["subordinating","reason"]),
        ("Choose the correct conjunction: ___ you apologize, I will not forgive you.", ["If","Unless","Because","Although"], "Unless", "'Unless' = 'if you do not apologize, I will not forgive you.'", ["subordinating","negative condition"]),
