        ("Choose the correct conjunction: ___ the penalty is harsh, it is commensurate with the gravity of the offense.", ["Granted that","Because","Since","In order that"], "Granted that", "'Granted that' = 'even though/admitting that' — concedes harshness but justifies it.", ["concessive","granted that","formal"]),
        ("Choose the correct conjunction: The regulation shall take effect ___ it is published in the Official Gazette.", ["until","once","unless","provided that"], "once", "'Once' = 'as soon as' — effectivity begins upon publication.", ["once","temporal trigger"]),
