        ("Choose the sentence with CORRECT modifier placement:", ["She has been working on the project for two years diligently.","She has been diligently working on the project for two years.","Diligently she has been working on the project for two years.","She has been working diligently on the project for two years."], "She has been diligently working on the project for two years.", "'Diligently' best modifies 'working' when placed before it or between auxiliary and main verb.", ["adverb placement","split infinitive"]),
        ("Identify the dangling modifier: 'Based on the evidence presented, the complaint is dismissed.'", ["Based on the evidence presented, the committee dismisses the complaint.","The complaint is dismissed based on the evidence presented.","Both A and B are acceptable corrections.","The sentence is acceptable in legal writing."], "The sentence is acceptable in legal writing.", "While technically a dangling modifier, 'based on' in this construction is widely accepted in legal/formal writing.", ["dangling modifier","accepted usage","legal writing"]),
