        ("Identify the dangling modifier: 'Required to attend the seminar, the office was left unattended for the entire day.'", ["Required to attend the seminar, the employees left the office unattended for the entire day.","The office was left unattended because the employees were required to attend the seminar.","Both A and B correctly fix the error.","The sentence is already correct."], "Both A and B correctly fix the error.", "'Required to attend the seminar' must modify people (employees), not 'the office.'", ["dangling modifier","past participle"]),
