        ("Identify the squinting modifier: 'The employee who was warned about tardiness repeatedly arrived late.'", ["The employee who was repeatedly warned about tardiness arrived late.","The employee who was warned about tardiness arrived late repeatedly.","Both A and B are valid interpretations.","The sentence is clear as written."], "Both A and B are valid interpretations.", "'Repeatedly' could modify 'warned' (warned many times) or 'arrived late' (late many times).", ["squinting modifier","adverb ambiguity"]),
        ("Identify the dangling modifier: 'Believing the information to be confidential, the documents were kept in a locked cabinet.'", ["Believing the information to be confidential, the officer kept the documents in a locked cabinet.","The documents were kept in a locked cabinet because the information was believed to be confidential.","Both A and B correctly fix the error.","The sentence is already correct."], "Both A and B correctly fix the error.", "'Believing' needs a human subject. 'The documents' cannot believe anything.", ["dangling modifier","present participle"]),
