        ("Identify the dangling modifier: 'Instructed to prioritize urgent matters, the routine paperwork was set aside.'", ["Instructed to prioritize urgent matters, the staff set aside the routine paperwork.","The routine paperwork was set aside because the staff was instructed to prioritize urgent matters.","Both A and B correctly fix the error.","The sentence is already correct."], "Both A and B correctly fix the error.", "'Instructed to prioritize' must modify people (the staff), not 'the routine paperwork.'", ["dangling modifier","past participle"]),
